db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "380e10d6-e728-562d-9721-3838f62a9783" :question/math-academy-id "q-102808" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3=y \\\\ 3y=4x+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ -4x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bccd7e22-9d2f-55d5-a585-963c2c52e8cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091452} {:answer/id #uuid "04d7a9f7-35c9-5204-a09d-ea360946c5af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091453} {:answer/id #uuid "393a819a-e9b9-5ced-86ec-c7f3f71d69a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091454} {:answer/id #uuid "552c169a-0af2-5304-8ad3-715fa39d203b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091455} {:answer/id #uuid "78071ddb-84be-5063-8e44-a7a8d21faf35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d7a9f7-35c9-5204-a09d-ea360946c5af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091453} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ebc66e-bfc3-563f-a5f0-6e3cfbfd3101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091451}] :question/id #uuid "a7ea58d8-c912-5e16-b0bd-a3c96b9a8c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8857" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n${2x = 5y; x =-2$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "effeafbf-2d74-5317-a2f1-82ffd2e09eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 